.TH DEXPIRECACHE 8 "2026-10-26"
.SH NAME
dexpirecache \- Diablo program to expire the dreaderd article cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dexpirecache
[
.B \-d
.I cachedir
]
[
.B \-f
.I kbytes
]
[
.B \-i
.I inodes
]
[
.B \-t
]
[
.B \-v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I dexpirecache
frees space in the article cache that dreaderd keeps when
.B readercache
is on (normally path_cache, /news/spool/cache).  When the file system
holding
.I cachedir
has less free space than
.B \-f
or fewer free inodes than
.BR \-i ,
it removes cache files, least recently used first (by access time),
until enough space is free.  Otherwise it does nothing.
.PP
The order depends on access times, so the cache file system should not
be mounted with noatime.
.PP
At the end it prints how many cache files it found and removed, split
into files read again after they were cached, files never read again,
and empty pre-cache files, and the age of the oldest and newest removed
file.  Run it from cron, for example every hour.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " cachedir"
The cache directory.  Default: path_cache from diablo.config
(/news/spool/cache).
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.TP
.BI \-f " kbytes"
Keep at least this many kilobytes free.
.TP
.BI \-i " inodes"
Keep at least this many inodes free.
.TP
.B \-t
Truncate cache files to zero length instead of removing them.
.TP
.B \-v
Be verbose.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dexpirecache -d /news/spool/cache -f 2000000 -i 100000
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
dreaderd(8),
dexpireover(8),
diablo-files(5)
